 - AMD Ryzen 7 4800HS with Radeon Graphics (16 threads) - 14.41 GiB memory\n> \n> And wasn't able to reproduce.\n\nAlso wanna mention I run a dual boot system, and just tried again while using Linux instead and had no issues. Despite the same hardware it is still broken on Windows.\n\n<img width=\"2548\" height=\"1426\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/dd7e8d92-6efe-4b90-a8a6-1dc391348e19\" />\n\nGodot v4.5.1.stable - TUXEDO OS 24.04.1 LTS on Wayland - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 2 monitors - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - AMD Radeon RX 7900 GRE (radeonsi, navi31, LLVM 17.0.6, DRM 3.61, 6.11.0-120029-tuxedo) - AMD Ryzen 7 7700X 8-Core Processor (16 threads) - 30.43 GiB memory\n\nConsidering your test used a discreet gpu on Linux, and integrated graphics on windows, suggests maybe the issue is windows only while using a discreet AMD gpu??","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3643711556/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3886996139","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113602#issuecomment-3886996139","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113602","id":3886996139,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7nrtqr","user":{"login":"brusteca","id":18575869,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NTc1ODY5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18575869?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brusteca","html_url":"https://github.com/brusteca","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brusteca/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brusteca/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brusteca/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brusteca/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brusteca/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brusteca/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brusteca/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brusteca/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brusteca/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-11T20:30:22Z","updated_at":"2026-02-11T20:31:12Z","body":"I ran into this issue after upgrading to Godot 4.6, with a Radeon RX7600 on Windows 10. Compatibility renderer, if I changed to Forward+ billboards would work fine. I only saw the issue on _some_ scenes, which was really puzzling. This is, I have a scene that contains a Sprite3D scene where billboarding works fine, and another scene where I plop the same Sprite3D scene and billboarding wouldn't work. Effectively as @TobySkateboard said, setting `fixed size = true` would fix the issue.\n\nI upgraded the drivers to 26.1.1 (released 2026-01-08) and the issue is seemingly gone (I was running version 25.something before, didn't note it down).","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3886996139/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]